    "result_text": "The test passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added **one place that lists every invoice across all projects**, showing each invoice's project name and lifecycle stage. The existing schema already had everything needed (invoices, projects, clients, `status` column), so no migration was required \u2014 the change was purely additive across the server and front-end.\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor REST):**\n- `InvoiceView.java` \u2014 a DTO carrying an invoice's id, project id, project **name**, amount, and status (the cross-entity join, done server-side).\n- `InvoiceRepository.findAllViews()` \u2014 a JPQL constructor query joining `Invoice` to `Project`, oldest id first.\n- `AllInvoicesGet.java` + `rest/api/invoices.GET.yml` \u2014 a new `GET /api/invoices` endpoint returning the list.\n\n**Front-end (all new files, additive):**\n- `features/invoices/queries.ts` \u2014 extended with an `AllInvoice` type, the `['invoices','all']` query key, and `fetchAllInvoices()`.\n- `features/invoices/AllInvoicesTable.tsx` \u2014 the table (`all-invoices-table`) with a row per invoice (`invoice-row-<id>`) exposing `invoice-project` and `invoice-status`.\n- `routes/invoices.tsx` \u2014 the `/invoices` page (flat, no detail views, so a single route file like the dashboard).\n- `features/invoices/all-nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `nav-invoices` shell link, auto-discovered via the slot glob.\n\nBoth `npm run typecheck` and the Playwright acceptance test pass.",
